      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The second claim follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/35F499" data-tag="35F499">5.4.5.5</a> and the dual result concerning limits. To prove the first, we observe that $\calX '$ is presentable by Proposition <a href="/tag/D930A9" data-tag="D930A9">5.5.3.12</a>. To show that $\calX $ is an $\infty $-topos, it will suffice to show that it satisfies criterion $(2)$ of Theorem <a href="/tag/5A32AA" data-tag="5A32AA">6.1.0.6</a>. This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/35F499" data-tag="35F499">5.4.5.5</a>, given that $\calX $ and $\calY '$ satisfy criterion $(2)$ of Theorem <a href="/tag/5A32AA" data-tag="5A32AA">6.1.0.6</a>. 
